# Dependencies

The runbook is `docs/DEPENDABOT_OPERATIONS.md`. This is the same factory standard used for road2media, foco-pets, and set-picks (2026-10-22). It replaces “never auto-merge a major.”

- Dependabot updates, majors included, auto-merge into `staging` when the required checks pass.
- A major that fails checks stays open. It is not merged. It becomes an `agent-queue` `p3` migration issue.
- Visitor-facing packages (React, React Router, Tailwind, the Firebase client SDK, icons, and the other names in `scripts/lib/dependabotAutoMergePolicy.mjs`) get the `ui-check` label. Patrick spot-checks staging before release. The label does not block the merge.
- `@types/node` ignores majors beyond the Node LTS this project runs. That version is `functions/package.json` `engines.node` (24). The ignore is `>=25.0.0` in `dependabot.yml`.
- Security updates are not grouped into the Monday batch. They auto-merge when checks pass.
- A quarterly workflow reminds us to check the Node and Vercel runtimes. It does not change them.
- Keep the `firebase-admin` major ignore in `/functions` until `firebase-functions-test` allows admin 14.

## Never

- `@dependabot rebase` the whole queue. Rebases are disabled on purpose.
- Bump `package.json` `version` on a Dependabot PR.
- Checkout or run the Dependabot pull request’s code from the auto-merge workflow. The token can write. Use `dependabot/fetch-metadata` and the policy script from the default branch.
- Turn on `alert-lookup` unless a personal access token is already available. Do not add a secret for it.
- Deploy Firebase, change Vercel settings, or edit branch protection from a dependency PR.

## When a lockfile breaks

- EUSAGE (lockfile out of sync): run `npm install` in that directory and push to the PR branch. Your push turns auto-merge off until Dependabot pushes again.
- ERESOLVE: check the upstream peer range before treating it as something you can force. `firebase-admin` 14 is the known case. Leave the ignore in place.
